CAT = "nlvcaLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
# SSVV VCA-ETT 3.0 (2026), section A.01 Regulations and safety rules: A.01.01 (NL and Belgian H&S law,
# environmental and working hours law, CE marking), A.01.01.01 inspectorate powers, A.01.01.03 health
# surveillance, A.01.02.01 employee duties and rights, A.01.02.05 employer duties, A.01.04.02
# agreements on safe working practices. Toetsmatrijs 2026: 4 of 40 per exam.
Q = [
("In the Dutch name Arbowet, what does the part \"Arbo\" refer to?",
 "Working conditions", ["Labour contracts", "Employment agencies", "Workplace pay scales"],
 "Arbo is short for arbeidsomstandigheden, working conditions. The Arbowet (Working Conditions Act) sets the health and safety duties of employers and employees in the Netherlands."),
("Which Belgian law protects the health and safety of employees at work?",
 "Welfare at Work Act", ["Working Conditions Act", "Environmental Management Act", "Working Hours Act"],
 "In Belgium the Welfare at Work Act (wet welzijn op het werk) is the basic law. The Working Conditions Act (Arbowet) is the Dutch equivalent."),
("In Belgium, what is the CODEX in health and safety law?",
 "Implementing decrees of the welfare law", ["Register of VCA-certified firms", "Code of conduct for site visitors", "Belgian list of approved PPE"],
 "The Codex on well-being at work gathers the implementing decrees of the Belgian Welfare at Work Act. It is not a firm register or a product list."),
("Which of these is an aim of health and safety legislation?",
 "Optimal working conditions", ["Shorter construction schedules", "Lower wage costs for employers", "Fewer state inspections"],
 "The ETT names three aims: protection while working, better health and safety at the workplace, and optimal working conditions. Cost and schedule are not aims of the law."),
("Under health and safety law, who counts as an employee?",
 "Trainees and volunteers too", ["Permanent staff only", "Staff with a written contract", "Workers aged 18 and over"],
 "The legislation covers the employer and all employees, including temporary agency workers, trainees and volunteers. A missing contract does not remove the protection."),
("Where does health and safety legislation apply?",
 "Every place where work is done", ["Only on construction sites", "Only inside company buildings", "Only where a permit is issued"],
 "The law applies at all locations where work is carried out, from a refinery to a client's house. A work permit is one way of agreeing safe work, not the limit of the law."),
("Besides safety and health, which third domain does health and safety law cover?",
 "Welfare", ["Productivity", "Quality control", "Profitability"],
 "The domains are safety, health and welfare (well-being). Quality and productivity are business goals, not domains of the law."),
("A Dutch company has no in-house prevention expertise. What must it do?",
 "Engage external expert support", ["Ask the Labour Inspectorate to help", "Let staff assess risks alone", "Wait for the next audit"],
 "In the Netherlands the company appoints one or more prevention officers, and where the expertise is not in-house it engages external support. The Labour Inspectorate enforces the law; it does not act as the company's adviser."),
("In Belgium, which prevention department must every employer set up?",
 "Internal prevention service (IDPBW)", ["External prevention service (EDPBW)", "Works council safety desk", "Regional inspectorate office"],
 "Every Belgian employer sets up an internal prevention and protection service with at least one prevention advisor. An external service (EDPBW) is engaged on top where the expertise is not available in-house."),
("Which is an objective of environmental legislation?",
 "Limit emissions and waste flows", ["Set maximum working hours", "Require CE marking on tools", "Cap the weight of loads lifted by hand"],
 "Environmental law protects people and the environment from harmful effects, limits emissions and waste flows and ensures waste is removed correctly. Working hours and CE marking come from other rules."),
("What is the main safety purpose of working hours legislation?",
 "Maximum hours and minimum rest", ["Overtime pay rates per sector", "Fixed start times on sites", "Holiday schedules per sector"],
 "Working hours law sets maximum working time and minimum rest so that tiredness does not endanger safety and health. It also aims at a balance between work, care and family life."),
("Who must attach the CE marking to work equipment?",
 "Manufacturer or importer", ["Employer who buys the equipment", "Labour Inspectorate", "VCA certification body"],
 "The manufacturer or importer attaches the CE marking and confirms in a declaration of conformity that the product meets the EU directive. The buyer and the inspectorate do not apply it."),
("What may you assume when PPE carries a CE marking?",
 "It meets EU safety requirements", ["It was inspected this year", "It fits every size of wearer", "It was made inside the EU"],
 "A CE marking means you may assume the product complies with the safety requirements of the European directive. It says nothing about periodic inspection, fit or the country of manufacture."),
("On which document may a manufacturer base a CE marking?",
 "Declaration of conformity", ["Yearly inspection sticker", "Employer's written approval", "Inspectorate test report"],
 "The CE marking may only be attached on the basis of a technical file and a declaration of conformity from the manufacturer or importer. Inspection stickers show periodic checks, not conformity."),
("An inspector finds people in serious danger on site. What may the Labour Inspectorate do?",
 "Halt the work on the spot", ["Dismiss the site manager", "Jail the employer on the spot", "Cancel workers' VCA diplomas"],
 "The inspectorate may halt work where people are in serious danger, draw up an official report and give warnings. Dismissing staff or sentencing people is not its power."),
("Which power does the Labour Inspectorate have during a site visit?",
 "Asking workers for their ID", ["Searching workers' homes", "Setting workers' hourly wages", "Issuing replacement VCA diplomas"],
 "Inspectors may ask employees for valid proof of identity, investigate accidents and set requirements for compliance. VCA diplomas come from recognised exam centres."),
("What right do employees have regarding health surveillance?",
 "Regular offer of a medical check", ["Free private healthcare for family", "Paid leave for any illness", "Access to colleagues' records"],
 "Employees regularly get the opportunity to take part in a medical examination to prevent and limit health risks. The right does not extend to other people's medical records."),
("Which is a general obligation of the employee under health and safety law?",
 "Report incidents to the supervisor", ["Draw up the written risk analysis", "Buy and maintain their own PPE", "Organise toolbox meetings"],
 "Employees must report incidents and serious danger to the supervisor. The risk analysis, providing PPE and organising meetings are the employer's duties."),
("A guard on a machine slows your work down. What does the law require of you?",
 "Keep it fitted and use it", ["Remove it if you are careful", "Adjust it to suit your pace", "Take it off with a colleague watching"],
 "Employees must not change or remove protective devices and must use them correctly. Care or a second person does not make a removed guard acceptable."),
("Which is a general right of the employee?",
 "Stopping work when people are in danger", ["Refusing any task they dislike doing", "Picking their own site supervisor", "Skipping training they already know well"],
 "The employee has the right to information and education, to a safe working environment and to interrupt work where people are in danger. Following training is a duty, not optional."),
("You face serious and immediate danger. Besides reporting it at once, what do you do?",
 "Stop and move to a safe place", ["Finish the task quickly", "Wait for written instructions", "Phone the Labour Inspectorate"],
 "With imminent serious danger you report it to the supervisor straight away, stop and go somewhere safe, and limit the consequences with your own knowledge and means. Waiting for paperwork wastes time."),
("Which is an obligation of the employer under health and safety law?",
 "Make a written risk analysis", ["Repair workers' private tools", "Approve CE markings", "Run the Central Diploma Register"],
 "The employer must make a written risk analysis, provide effective protective equipment, arrange instruction and plan for assistance and evacuation. CE marking is the manufacturer's task."),
("In Belgium, which insurance must employers take out for all employees?",
 "Occupational accident insurance", ["Private vehicle insurance", "Tool theft insurance", "Legal expenses insurance"],
 "Belgian employers must insure all employees against occupational accidents. The other policies are optional business choices."),
("On a Dutch building site, how are agreements on safe working practices usually made?",
 "Via the site supervisor (uitvoerder)", ["Through a petrochemical work permit", "By email to the Labour Inspectorate office", "At the yearly works council meeting"],
 "In construction you report to the site supervisor (uitvoerder) and make the agreements with them; in petrochemicals a work permit records them and in cleaning a work sheet. The inspectorate is not part of the daily agreement."),
("Which item belongs in an agreement on safe working practices?",
 "Its validity period", ["Workers' home addresses", "Price of the contract", "Workers' pay scales"],
 "The agreement lists the safety-critical work, location, measures and PPE, date and duration, its validity period, duties and contact details. Prices and pay are not part of it."),
("What is the operational employee's task under the agreements for safe working?",
 "Comply with the agreed measures", ["Accept the residual risks for the site", "Authorise the start of the work", "Set the validity period"],
 "Operational employees must know the agreements and comply with the agreed conditions and measures. Authorising the work and accepting residual risks lie with the person responsible on site."),
]
